From 751aced9303ca17ffff290c0c0f9191b89bff86b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 03:41:24 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Show a 3D video in 3D through the compositor, in a window
 of its own

Under a Wayland compositor that takes stereo content declarations
(kde_stereo_content_v1, with wl_subcompositor, wp_viewporter and wl_shm), the monitor
menu's Stereoscopic 3D > Preview gets a 3D Window entry. It opens a window that shows
what the monitor shows in 3D: the two views of each frame, whatever the packing the
project or the clip has (frame sequences are shown as they are), side by side at the
size of the window with the left eye first, in a surface under the window's, declared
as full side by side. Qt creates subsurfaces only above their parent, so the layer is a
wl_subsurface made in StereoPreview. The window is transparent over it; the monitors
keep the controls and the packed frame, the same in both eyes.

It is built only where the dependencies are there (STEREO_PREVIEW, on by default:
wayland-client, the viewporter protocol, libstereo-declare, Qt's private GUI headers),
and offered only when the compositor has what it needs.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet via Claude Code
